{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/stage-a-reader-brief.md /Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/dryrun11/packet.json'","aggregated_output":"# Stage A reading form: is each answer a sound judged question for its thesis, or a justified refusal? (read-only)\n\nYou are an independent reader. Do not edit files, run model calls or start runs. Do not read any other reader's answers.\n\n## What you are reading\n\nThe packet you are given holds a list of items. Each item is one research topic (\"thesis\") a system opened\nwhile reading one news article, with a proposed **judged question** for it:\n- `thesis`: the fields the system wrote when it opened the topic: `description` (the topic's wording), `outcome` (what is tracked),\n  `period`, `opens_as`, `settled_by`;\n- `article`: the opening article's publication date, title and full text;\n- `fiscal_year_note`: how the company names its fiscal years and which is this year and which next year on the article's day,\n  the same note the step was given. Use it wherever a mark turns on a year;\n- `ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it`: the proposed judged question exactly as a later judge will see it: its `object` (the company's\n  ticker NVDA, or a theme id), `kind`, its `focus` (the line the judge is shown beside the question: the thesis's `outcome`),\n  `question`, `year`, `due_day` and its `rungs` (each a label and a condition; exactly one rung\n  is meant to hold on the due day). Or `no_ladder` with a reason: the step declined to write a question;\n- `other_fields`: what the step recorded beside the ladder and the judge does not see: `not_judged` (parts of the topic's wording\n  the question leaves out, with why), `reference` (what the article says the market expects, quoted, with its number when the article states\n  one; when it has a number, the judge also sees the quoted passage, inside the middle rung's condition), `favourable_end`,\n  `due_day_basis`.\n\nSome items are sound and some carry a fault. Judge each on its own against its thesis and its article.\n\n## The rules a judged question must meet\n\n- One judged question asks **one** figure for a named period or **one** event: the one the thesis's `outcome` names. Every other\n  part of the thesis's wording that the question leaves out (a second figure or event, a condition, a comparison) must be listed\n  in `not_judged`.\n- A yes/no event has two rungs, Yes and No; an event with more states, or a figure, has five. Exactly one rung holds for every\n  possible outcome: no overlap, no gap.\n- A question about the company's revenue, profit, share, product progress or its own obligations is the company's (object NVDA,\n  kind asset). A question about what happens in the world (licensing, aggregate spending, a policy) is a theme's.\n- A company's five-rung ladder runs from Strongly bullish to Strongly bearish, meaning good or bad for the company's business.\n- The reference is what the market expects for the question when it opens: a consensus, the company's guidance, a stated plan or\n  deadline. When the article states it as a number, the `reference` field carries that number and a figure's middle rung holds it.\n  When the article states it in words alone, the field carries the words and no number, and the ranges are the step's own\n  estimate.\n- The due day is when the question can be resolved: a figure's publication date; for an event, the date its outcome is assessed. Where\n  the thesis or the article states the day a figure is published, that day is right; where neither does, a plausible reporting\n  date after the period ends is right.\n- A company's figure for a quarter or a half-year is never a judged question: the step must decline it. A ladder written for\n  one is wrong even when it asks exactly what the thesis names (mark `Y`). An annual figure that only names quarterly reports as\n  the material that settles it is not such a case.\n- A step may decline (`no_ladder`) only in the six cases its instructions allow: the thesis has no main figure or event (its\n  outcome names several things and none is the main one); nothing in it can be checked on a date; it is the company's figure for a\n  quarter or a half-year; it is a figure for a year that had already ended on the article's day; it is a figure for a year beyond\n  next year, unless the thesis's `opens_as` is binding_obligation; or the question belongs to another company, or to a matter that\n  none of the listed themes covers (the listed themes are given with the packet). Declining for any other reason, or when the case\n  named does not truly apply, is not justified.\n\n## What to return\n\nOne JSON object per item, one per line, in item order, as your final message: no prose before or after, no code fence. Fields:\n\n| field | values | the mark |\n|---|---|---|\n| `item` | the item number | |\n| `Q` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the judged question is worded as a question, not as an assertion, and asks the thing the thesis's `outcome` names. For a figure it also names the period the figure covers, or the day it is measured at, and the material that settles it. And it does not ask something other than its `focus` line (a focus that also names parts listed in `not_judged` is expected and is not a conflict). `n/a` for a `no_ladder` |\n| `O` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the object is the question's own company or the right theme |\n| `R` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | exactly one rung holds for every outcome; for a yes/no, the Yes condition is the event happening and the No condition its complement. Every condition is concrete and can be checked on the due day: none rests on a target or a threshold that is not yet set |\n| `D` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the due day follows the rule for its kind. A figure: a day by which the figure can be expected to have been published, after its period ends (the day the thesis or the article states, or, where neither states one, a plausible reporting date). An event: the date the thesis or the article gives for assessing it, or the last day of the period it names, or the company's fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision with no date. It fails when the day contradicts a date the thesis or the article gives, falls before the figure's period ends, or, for an event, is a date none of these gives And `due_day_basis` says truly where the day comes from: `stated` only when the thesis or the article gives that day; `period_end` only when it is the last day of the period the thesis names, or the fiscal year-end for a pending regulatory decision; `expected_publication` when the step set the day it expects the figure to be published |\n| `X` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | where the article states what the market expects for this quantity or event, the ladder places it rightly (a figure: the stated number lies in the middle rung; an expectation in words alone cannot be placed and holds); where the article states none, it holds unless the ladder claims one |\n| `F` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a five-rung ladder about the company only: the direction is defensible (which end is bullish, or the labels of the states). For a figure, the reason given in `favourable_why` supports the favourable end. For five states, the Neutral state's condition says what it is neutral against: the expected outcome when the article states one, otherwise a baseline it names. `n/a` for a yes/no ladder and for a theme |\n| `Y` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a figure only: the year, the unit and the scale of the numbers are the question's (an amount in full; a percentage as 31, not 0.31), and the figure is a whole year's. A company's figure for a quarter or a half-year fails, whatever the thesis asks |\n| `G` | `holds`, `fails`, `not_assessable`, `n/a` | for a figure, always one of the first three: where the article gives any figure for this quantity, `holds` when an analyst would accept the ranges as a fair division of the outcomes around it and `fails` when not; `not_assessable` when the article gives none. `n/a` only for an event's ladder and for a `no_ladder` |\n| `L` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | every other part of the thesis's wording that the question leaves out (a second figure or event, a condition, a comparison) is listed in `not_judged`, each with a reason that says why it is left out; a wording that asks nothing else holds with an empty list |\n| `B` | a list | exactly one entry for each part listed in `not_judged`, in its order: `\"bet\"` when an analyst would hold a separate view on it, `\"not_a_bet\"` when it is a detail of the judged question; `[]` when nothing is listed and for a `no_ladder` |\n| `XR` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | the `reference` field quotes what the article states the market expects. It carries the number when the article states one, and no number the article does not state. (The one case where a stated number is rightly left out: it cannot be written within the step's limits, zero or a size from a billionth to a billion billion with at most fifteen significant digits. $17.2 billion can; 2.5 quintillion dollars cannot.) It is null only when the article states no expectation |\n| `N` | `holds`, `fails`, `n/a` | for a `no_ladder` only: the refusal is justified by one of the allowed cases, and that case truly applies. A refusal because the question belongs to another company or to a matter no listed theme covers names that company or matter. Which year is this year and which next year is read from the `fiscal_year_note` |\n| `W` | a string | any other fault that would mislead a reader of this judged question, in a short sentence; the empty string `\"\"` when there is none. The field is always present |\n| `why` | a string | one sentence giving the reason for every `fails` and for a non-empty `W`, naming the words or the figure; it may be empty only when no mark fails and `W` is empty |\n\nRead each item's article before answering it. Judge only what is in the item.\n[\n {\n  \"item\": 1,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027 after lifting its outlook?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart lifts full-year revenue outlook\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) raised its full-year outlook on Thursday, saying it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, up from the $16.8 billion it guided in March. New stores in the south-west opened ahead of plan. Shares rose 3%.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"question\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for FY2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, in its fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-15\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"18,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 17,500,000,000 USD to below 18,000,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,900,000,000 USD to below 17,500,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,400,000,000 USD to below 16,900,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 16,400,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 17200000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"Higher revenue is good for the grocer's business.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"stated\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 2,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"How will the competition regulator decide on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"period\": \"By 31 March 2027, the deadline the regulator set.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The regulator's published decision.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"Regulator opens in-depth review of GreenCart-FreshWay deal\",\n   \"text\": \"The competition regulator opened an in-depth review of GreenCart Grocers' (GRCR) purchase of FreshWay Foods and set a deadline of 31 March 2027 for its decision. The regulator gave no indication of its thinking. GreenCart said it would cooperate fully.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the competition regulator have decided on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods by 2027-03-31, as shown by its published decision?\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with no conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has not withdrawn its filing.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has withdrawn its filing.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has blocked the purchase.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": null,\n   \"favourable_end\": null,\n   \"favourable_why\": null,\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"stated\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 3,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027 after lifting its outlook?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart lifts full-year revenue outlook\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) raised its full-year outlook on Thursday, saying it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, up from the $16.8 billion it guided in March. New stores in the south-west opened ahead of plan. Shares rose 3%.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"question\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for FY2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, in its fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-15\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"18,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 17,500,000,000 USD to below 18,000,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,900,000,000 USD to below 17,500,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,400,000,000 USD to below 16,900,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 16,400,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 17200000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"Higher revenue is good for the grocer's business.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 4,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What gross margin will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 gross margin, against its guidance of about 31%.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart guides gross margin to about 31%\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) said it expects a gross margin of about 31% for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, as own-label sales grow. Last year's margin was 30.2%.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 gross margin, against its guidance of about 31%.\",\n   \"question\": \"What gross margin will GreenCart report for FY2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, in its annual report?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"0.33 percent or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 0.32 percent to below 0.33 percent\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 0.3 percent to below 0.32 percent (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it expects a gross margin of about 31% for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 0.29 percent to below 0.3 percent\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 0.29 percent\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it expects a gross margin of about 31% for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 0.31\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"A higher gross margin leaves the grocer more profit on each sale.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 5,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027 after lifting its outlook?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart lifts full-year revenue outlook\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) raised its full-year outlook on Thursday, saying it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, up from the $16.8 billion it guided in March. New stores in the south-west opened ahead of plan. Shares rose 3%.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"question\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for FY2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, in its fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-15\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"18,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 17,500,000,000 USD to below 18,000,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,900,000,000 USD to below 17,500,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,400,000,000 USD to below 16,900,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 16,400,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 17200000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"GreenCart's fiscal year ends in January.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 6,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will GreenCart's loyalty scheme reach its sign-up goal by the end of 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether the Basket loyalty scheme reaches 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026.\",\n   \"period\": \"By 31 December 2026, the date GreenCart gives.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's own report of sign-ups.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart launches loyalty scheme with a five-million target\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) launched its Basket loyalty scheme on Thursday and said it aims for 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026. Chief executive Mara Olsen said management would review the scheme's goals again at the September trading update.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"Whether the Basket loyalty scheme reaches 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026.\",\n   \"question\": \"Will the Basket loyalty scheme have reached its sign-up goal by 2026-12-31, as reported by GreenCart?\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"Sign-ups have reached whatever target management confirms at its September trading update.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"Sign-ups have not reached whatever target management confirms at its September trading update.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it aims for 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026\",\n    \"value\": null\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": null,\n   \"favourable_why\": null,\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"stated\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 7,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"How will the competition regulator decide on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"period\": \"By 31 March 2027, the deadline the regulator set.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The regulator's published decision.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"Regulator opens in-depth review of GreenCart-FreshWay deal\",\n   \"text\": \"The competition regulator opened an in-depth review of GreenCart Grocers' (GRCR) purchase of FreshWay Foods and set a deadline of 31 March 2027 for its decision. Analysts widely expect the deal to be cleared on condition that GreenCart sells stores in overlapping towns. GreenCart said it would cooperate fully.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the competition regulator have decided on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods by 2027-03-31, as shown by its published decision?\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with no conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has not withdrawn its filing: the review is still open, short of the clearance with store sales that analysts expect.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has withdrawn its filing.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has blocked the purchase.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"Analysts widely expect the deal to be cleared on condition that GreenCart sells stores in overlapping towns\",\n    \"value\": null\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": null,\n   \"favourable_why\": null,\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"stated\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 8,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What gross margin will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 gross margin, against its guidance of about 31%.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart guides gross margin to about 31%\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) said it expects a gross margin of about 31% for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, as own-label sales grow. Last year's margin was 30.2%.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 gross margin, against its guidance of about 31%.\",\n   \"question\": \"What gross margin will GreenCart report for FY2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, in its annual report?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"33 percent or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 32 percent to below 33 percent\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 30 percent to below 32 percent (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it expects a gross margin of about 31% for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 29 percent to below 30 percent\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 29 percent\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it expects a gross margin of about 31% for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 31\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"A higher gross margin leaves the grocer more profit on each sale.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 9,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027 after lifting its outlook?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart lifts full-year revenue outlook\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) raised its full-year outlook on Thursday, saying it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, up from the $16.8 billion it guided in March. New stores in the south-west opened ahead of plan. Shares rose 3%.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"question\": \"GreenCart will report FY2027 revenue, for the year ending 30 January 2027, above its guidance in its fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report.\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-15\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"18,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 17,500,000,000 USD to below 18,000,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,900,000,000 USD to below 17,500,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,400,000,000 USD to below 16,900,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 16,400,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 17200000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"Higher revenue is good for the grocer's business.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 10,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"How will the competition regulator decide on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"period\": \"By 31 March 2027, the deadline the regulator set.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The regulator's published decision.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"Regulator opens in-depth review of GreenCart-FreshWay deal\",\n   \"text\": \"The competition regulator opened an in-depth review of GreenCart Grocers' (GRCR) purchase of FreshWay Foods and set a deadline of 31 March 2027 for its decision. The regulator gave no indication of its thinking. GreenCart said it would cooperate fully.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the competition regulator have decided on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods by 2027-03-31, as shown by its published decision?\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with no conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has not withdrawn its filing: the review stands where it stood on the article's day.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has withdrawn its filing.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has blocked the purchase.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": null,\n   \"favourable_end\": null,\n   \"favourable_why\": null,\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"stated\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 11,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for fiscal 2027 after lifting its outlook?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"period\": \"Fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report for fiscal 2027.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart lifts full-year revenue outlook\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) raised its full-year outlook on Thursday, saying it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, up from the $16.8 billion it guided in March. New stores in the south-west opened ahead of plan. Shares rose 3%.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"GreenCart's fiscal 2027 revenue, against its guidance of about $17.2 billion.\",\n   \"question\": \"What revenue will GreenCart report for FY2027, the year ending 30 January 2027, in its fourth-quarter earnings release and annual report?\",\n   \"year\": \"FY2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-15\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"18,000,000,000 USD or more\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 17,500,000,000 USD to below 18,000,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,900,000,000 USD to below 17,500,000,000 USD (the reference when the question opened: \\\"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\\\")\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"from 16,400,000,000 USD to below 16,900,000,000 USD\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"below 16,400,000,000 USD\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it now expects revenue of about $17.2 billion for fiscal 2027\",\n    \"value\": 17200000000\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": \"higher\",\n   \"favourable_why\": \"Higher revenue is good for the grocer's business.\",\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"expected_publication\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 12,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"Will GreenCart's loyalty scheme reach its sign-up goal by the end of 2026?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"Whether the Basket loyalty scheme reaches 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026.\",\n   \"period\": \"By 31 December 2026, the date GreenCart gives.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"product_node\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"GreenCart's own report of sign-ups.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"GreenCart launches loyalty scheme with a five-million target\",\n   \"text\": \"GreenCart Grocers (GRCR) launched its Basket loyalty scheme on Thursday and said it aims for 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026. Chief executive Mara Olsen said management would review the scheme's goals again at the September trading update.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"Whether the Basket loyalty scheme reaches 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026.\",\n   \"question\": \"Will the Basket loyalty scheme have reached its sign-up goal by 2026-12-31, as reported by GreenCart?\",\n   \"year\": \"2026\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2026-12-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Yes\",\n     \"condition\": \"GreenCart has reported at least 5,000,000 Basket sign-ups reached on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"No\",\n     \"condition\": \"GreenCart has not reported 5,000,000 Basket sign-ups reached on or before 2026-12-31.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"it aims for 5 million sign-ups by 31 December 2026\",\n    \"value\": null\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": null,\n   \"favourable_why\": null,\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"stated\"\n  }\n },\n {\n  \"item\": 13,\n  \"thesis\": {\n   \"description\": \"How will the competition regulator decide on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods?\",\n   \"outcome\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"period\": \"By 31 March 2027, the deadline the regulator set.\",\n   \"opens_as\": \"policy_stage\",\n   \"settled_by\": \"The regulator's published decision.\"\n  },\n  \"article\": {\n   \"publication_date\": \"2026-07-10\",\n   \"publisher\": \"retailwire.example\",\n   \"title\": \"Regulator opens in-depth review of GreenCart-FreshWay deal\",\n   \"text\": \"The competition regulator opened an in-depth review of GreenCart Grocers' (GRCR) purchase of FreshWay Foods and set a deadline of 31 March 2027 for its decision. Analysts widely expect the deal to be cleared on condition that GreenCart sells stores in overlapping towns. GreenCart said it would cooperate fully.\"\n  },\n  \"fiscal_year_note\": \"GRCR's fiscal year ends in January and is named for the calendar year in which it ends: FY2027 runs from February 2026 to January 2027. On 2026-07-10 this year is FY2027 and next year is FY2028.\",\n  \"ladder_as_the_judge_is_shown_it\": {\n   \"object\": \"GRCR\",\n   \"kind\": \"asset\",\n   \"focus\": \"The regulator's decision on the FreshWay purchase by its 31 March 2027 deadline.\",\n   \"question\": \"What will the competition regulator have decided on GreenCart's purchase of FreshWay Foods by 2027-03-31, as shown by its published decision?\",\n   \"year\": \"2027\",\n   \"due_day\": \"2027-03-31\",\n   \"rungs\": [\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with no conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bullish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has cleared the purchase with conditions.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Neutral\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has not withdrawn its filing.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"No decision has been announced and GreenCart has withdrawn its filing.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"label\": \"Strongly bearish\",\n     \"condition\": \"The regulator has blocked the purchase.\"\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  \"other_fields\": {\n   \"not_judged\": [],\n   \"reference\": {\n    \"words\": \"Analysts widely expect the deal to be cleared on condition that GreenCart sells stores in overlapping towns\",\n    \"value\": null\n   },\n   \"favourable_end\": null,\n   \"favourable_why\": null,\n   \"due_day_basis\": \"stated\"\n  }\n }\n]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":1,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"fails\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The article and thesis do not state 15 March 2027 as a publication date, so its basis is not stated.\"}\n{\"item\":2,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"fails\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The Neutral condition does not name a baseline against which the open review is neutral.\"}\n{\"item\":3,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}\n{\"item\":4,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"fails\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"fails\",\"G\":\"fails\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"fails\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The middle range of 0.3% to below 0.32% excludes the 31% guidance, the ranges use the wrong percentage scale and are not a fair division around it, and the reference records 0.31 instead of 31.\"}\n{\"item\":5,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"fails\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The fiscal year ending in January does not explain why higher revenue is favourable.\"}\n{\"item\":6,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"fails\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"fails\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The rungs use a target that management has not yet confirmed instead of the stated 5 million sign-ups, and the reference omits that number.\"}\n{\"item\":7,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}\n{\"item\":8,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}\n{\"item\":9,\"Q\":\"fails\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The wording asserts that revenue will exceed guidance instead of asking what revenue will be reported.\"}\n{\"item\":10,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}\n{\"item\":11,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"holds\",\"Y\":\"holds\",\"G\":\"holds\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"\"}\n{\"item\":12,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"fails\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"n/a\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"fails\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"No report of 5 million sign-ups does not establish that the scheme failed to reach 5 million, and the reference omits that number.\"}\n{\"item\":13,\"Q\":\"holds\",\"O\":\"holds\",\"R\":\"holds\",\"D\":\"holds\",\"X\":\"holds\",\"F\":\"fails\",\"Y\":\"n/a\",\"G\":\"n/a\",\"L\":\"holds\",\"B\":[],\"XR\":\"holds\",\"N\":\"n/a\",\"W\":\"\",\"why\":\"The Neutral condition does not say that it is assessed against the expected clearance with store sales.\"}"}}
